{
  "rules": [
    "When recent history shows a sharp spike followed by zero sentiment, the model exhibits severe upward bias and fails to capture immediate mean reversion; apply a downward correction of 10-15% on the first forecast day.",
    "The model consistently underestimates volatility during high-sentiment or neutral periods, failing to account for sudden reversals after price peaks; reduce forecasted upside by approximately 20% when recent highs are followed by flat sentiment.",
    "In low-sentiment environments with volatile history, the model displays significant lag in recognizing downward trends, resulting in over-forecasting stability; apply a negative bias correction of -5 to -10 EUR per day for the first week.",
    "The model assumes linear continuation after spikes but true outcomes show rapid mean reversion within 3-5 days; reduce the slope of the forecast curve by 40% immediately following any single-day price increase."
  ]
}
